[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3627260493","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113619#issuecomment-3627260493","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113619","id":3627260493,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YM5pN","user":{"login":"ydeltastar","id":133662278,"node_id":"U_kgDOB_eGRg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/133662278?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar","html_url":"https://github.com/ydeltastar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-08T14:42:05Z","updated_at":"2025-12-08T14:42:05Z","body":"The history tracking is still inconsistent when jumping to symbols or navigating back. Several functions, `_save_history()`, `_save_previous_state()`, `_go_to_tab()`, and `_update_history_pos()`; conflict with each other by writing overlapping entries to the history timeline or mixing past and present states, tabs and script lines.\r\n\r\nFor example, when jumping to a symbol in another script, `_go_to_tab()` writes the current state and then creates a new entry to the tab without a state (meaning the start of the script), then `_save_history()` adds another entry with a state, resulting in a history of `current_line > first_line > current_line` for a simple jump.\r\n\r\nWhen moving back, `_update_history_pos()`, which should only read history, unexpectedly writes an entry too before moving to the previous one. `_save_previous_state()` also does its own thing, writing two entries to the history.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3627260493/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3627313768","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113619#issuecomment-3627313768","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113619","id":3627313768,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YNGpo","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-08T14:54:27Z","updated_at":"2025-12-08T14:54:27Z","body":"I'm aware but it is not the point of this PR to address that. This perma locking thi